{
  "@note": "Not a real ROM: a 512-byte option ROM stub (signature, length 1, and a RETF init entry) at 0xC0000 that lets an IBM PC AT with no video adapter (CMOS display type 00, the EGA/none setting) pass POST without a 162 configuration error, since the AT BIOS requires a video ROM for that setting; POST then leaves INT 10h pointing at its dummy IRET.",
  "width": 8,
